ination to give their time or material will have the satisfaction of knowing they helped. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stunned", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very surprised", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We were stunned by their sense of caring.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "zone", "type": "name"}, {"content": "area", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you want to help the victims in the hurricane zone, rely on  the people at A Helping Hand to make sure whatever your donation is, it is a meaningful one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in short supply ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having less than what is required", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is essential to know whatever is in short supply. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "protein-rich", "type": "name"}, {"content": "containing high levels of protein", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  At this point, medical supplies and protein-rich food are are needed, so whichever you choose to give will be used.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "diapers", "type": "name"}, {"content": "material wrapped around a baby's bottom and between its legs to absorb and retain bodily waste", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We had far too much clothing, for example, and not nearly enough diapers, blankets, and \u2013 odd as it sounds \u2013 toothpaste.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le14ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Relative Clauses: <span class=\"italic\">Whatever</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Whoever </span>and <span class=\"italic\">Whichever</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use relative clauses to define the noun that precedes it. It adds more detail and makes your writing or speech more sophisticated.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use some clauses beginning with <span class=\"italic\">whatever</span>, <span class=\"italic\">whoever </span>and <span class=\"italic\">whichever</span> to talk about people or things that are indefinite or unknown.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Whatever </span>means anything or it doesn't really matter. <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Whoever </span>means the person or group who/ any person or group. <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Whichever</span> means one thing or person from a limited number.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I'm sure I'll enjoy eating <span class=\"strong\">whatever you make</span>. </span><br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Whoever wins </span>will go on to play Spain in the final.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Whichever one of you </span>broke the vase will have to replace it.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you want to help the victims in the hurricane zone, rely on  the people at A Helping Hand to make sure <span class=\"strong\">whatever </span>your donation is, it is a meaningful one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You bless <span class=\"strong\">whoever </span>it was that gives you new things. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " At t