of natural disasters rely heavily on help from disaster relief organizations for which a range of supplies and support are provided by the public. The victims are grateful for whatever is made available. Whoever has the inclination to give their time or material will have the satisfaction of knowing they helped.\n<br>\nHow can you help?\n<br>\nTake a tip from Joan Hazelton, a hurricane survivor.<br>\"When I used to make donations to the needy, I quickly searched the house for things we no longer needed. I never thought of buying something new. But when our own family became the victims of a hurricane, you bless whoever it was that gives you new things. We were stunned by their sense of caring.\""}, {"time": "43000", "image": "engenn10le14ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "A Helping Hand is a charity to which you can give your help, time or money. However, there are certain items that are more in demand than others. One volunteer said,\n\u201cWe had far too much clothing, for example, and not nearly enough diapers, blankets, and \u2013 odd as it sounds \u2013 toothpaste. If you want to help the victims in the hurricane zone, rely on  the people at A Helping Hand to make sure whatever your donation is, it is a meaningful one.\u201d\n<br>\nIt is essential to know whatever is in short supply.  At this point, medical supplies and protein-rich food are needed so whichever you choose to give will be used.  Donations of clothing and tents are no longer required as there was a huge response to those who needed those items last week."}, {"time": "88000", "image": "engenn10le14ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Volunteer doctors, nurses and social workers who have flown in from various parts of the country to help are taking care of people whose lives have been threatened by infection or disease. At this point, we are looking for long-distance help and hoping you will respond. Whatever donations you give are crucial to us as they save lives. You might be happy to know we will give you a tax receipt for your kind monetary donations."}]}}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}